## MCP vs CLI

| Task | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `vercel link`, `vercel env ls` / `add` / `rm` | **CLI only** (MCP has no env-var tools) |
| Logs, inspect, list deployments | MCP (`get_project`, `list_deployments`, `get_deployment`) |
| Redeploy after env change | CLI `vercel redeploy <existing-production-url>` |

`list_projects` on this team returns many apps; pick `restaurant-system` /
`prj_wFVDqQOtf6cjuUXscIoHDbtHzTTz` (git `ralfcam/restaurant-system`). A
narrow MCP grant that omits this project 404s/403s — re-authorize rather
than inventing another id.

## Do not

- Do not `create_git_project` (409 — already linked).
- Do not retarget `syntex-global` / `prj_oWhr772lrsaNsUKWhpa0FAgle2p4`
  (`ralfcam/Syntex-V0`).
- Do not treat v0 `prj_Be4qMWXY4RzLyIZOq2jgTicLj4CO` or
  `next-js-restaurant-system-mvp.vercel.app` as this app’s host.
- Do not `npx vercel --prod` or MCP `deploy_to_vercel` to set env — that
  uploads a new tree and bypasses the git link.
- Do not point production at local Docker keys (`127.0.0.1:54321`). Hosted
  backend is Supabase `tilcqrudqxznnpepxjqq`.
- Do not print `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in chat or commits. `.vercel/` stays
  gitignored.
- Do not add `vercel.json` `crons` as the default timer. Scheduled jobs
  consider Supabase Edge Function + `pg_cron` first
  ([scheduled-jobs.mdc](.cursor/rules/scheduled-jobs.mdc)).

Env targets: **production and preview** for `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`,
`NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`.
